.TH "YOMI-CLI" "1" "September 2026" "yomi-cli" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
yomi-cli \- search and watch anime from the command line
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B yomi-cli
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIQUERY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B yomi-cli
searches anime through AniList metadata, resolves playback through Yomi.to and MegaPlay, and launches a local media player.
.PP
The command supports subbed and dubbed playback, quality selection, persistent subtitle preferences, episode history, downloads, and player integrations.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-c, --continue\fR
Continue watching from history.
.TP
\fB\-d, --download\fR
Download the episode instead of playing it.
.TP
\fB\-D, --delete\fR
Delete episode history.
.TP
\fB\-e, --episode, -r, --range\fR \fI<episode>\fR
Specify an episode or range. Use 0 for the first available episode and -1 for the last.
.TP
\fB\-l, --logview\fR
Show playback logs.
.TP
\fB\-q, --quality\fR \fI<best|worst|360|480|720|1080>\fR
Select video quality. The default is best.
.TP
\fB\-s, --syncplay\fR
Use Syncplay to watch with friends.
.TP
\fB\-S, --select-nth\fR \fI<index>\fR
Select the nth search or history entry.
.TP
\fB\-v, --vlc\fR
Use VLC as the media player.
.TP
\fB\-V, --version\fR
Show the script version.
.TP
\fB\-h, --help\fR
Show usage and options.
.TP
\fB\-N, --nextep-countdown\fR
Display a countdown to the next episode.
.TP
\fB\--dub\fR
Play the dubbed version. Subbed playback is the default.
.TP
\fB\--rofi\fR
Use rofi instead of fzf for interactive menus.
.TP
\fB\--dmenu\fR
Use dmenu instead of fzf for interactive menus.
.TP
\fB\--skip\fR
Use ani-skip to skip the intro when using mpv.
.TP
\fB\--no-detach\fR
Do not detach the player. Useful for terminal playback with mpv.
.TP
\fB\--exit-after-play\fR
Return after the player exits and use its exit code. Useful for non-interactive runs.
.SH INTERACTIVE MENU
After playback, the episode menu provides next, replay, previous, episode selection, quality selection, subtitle selection, and quit.
.PP
Navigation actions are queued until the current player exits. Subtitle selection offers available tracks and an off option. Subtitles start enabled and prefer English; the selected state is saved in the history directory.
.PP
For airing series whose total episode count is not published by AniList, the currently released episodes are derived from the next scheduled episode.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_MODE\fR
Playback mode: sub or dub. Default is sub.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_QUALITY\fR
Playback quality: best, worst, or a listed height. Default is best.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_PLAYER\fR
Player command or special player name. Default is platform dependent.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_PLAYER_FLAGS\fR
Additional player flags. Default is empty.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_MENU\fR
Menu frontend: fzf, rofi, dmenu, or another compatible command. Default is fzf.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_MENU_FLAGS\fR
Additional menu flags. Default is empty.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_HIST_DIR\fR
Directory for history and subtitle settings. Default is $XDG_STATE_HOME/yomi-cli or $HOME/.local/state/yomi-cli.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_DEFAULT_SOURCE\fR
Default source: search or history. Default is search.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_SUBTITLES\fR
Whether subtitles start enabled. Set to 0 or 1. Default is 1.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_SUBTITLE_LANGUAGE\fR
Initial preferred subtitle label. Default is English.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_RELAY_SCRIPT\fR
Path to yomi-relay.py. By default it is located beside yomi-cli.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_DOWNLOAD_DIR\fR
Directory for downloads. Default is the current directory.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_LOG\fR
Playback logging toggle. Set to 0 or 1. Default is 1.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_SKIP_INTRO\fR
Whether to use ani-skip. Set to 0 or 1. Default is 0.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_NO_DETACH\fR
Whether the player remains attached. Default is 0.
.TP
\fBYOMI_CLI_EXIT_AFTER_PLAY\fR
Whether to return after playback. Default is 0.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/yomi-cli/yomi-hsts\fR (or $HOME/.local/state/yomi-cli/yomi-hsts)
Episode history.
.TP
\fB$XDG_STATE_HOME/yomi-cli/settings\fR (or $HOME/.local/state/yomi-cli/settings)
Subtitle enabled state and preferred language.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
The normal path requires a POSIX shell, curl, sed, grep, jq, fzf or another menu frontend, Python 3, OpenSSL, and a compatible media player. Downloads additionally require yt-dlp or ffmpeg.
